    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0122', 'APG-S04-DS001', 'heading 2', '14.1 Data readiness — mandatory', 'C07'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0122', 'APG-S04-DS002', 'paragraph', 'Maintain a readiness record for each insight (detection rule, financial figure, market figure and any later insight) and the scope it applies to: a project, the organisation, a supplier, the portfolio or external data. It states the insight\'s state from its own gate (eligible, qualified, blocked or unavailable) and, for each input, how far it has reached: capture available, validation available, authority established, reconciliation available, decision-eligible. An insight is never shown as eligible while an input it needs is missing, unverified or stale; a conflicting or non-authoritative input counts as not verified (§5, §9). An insight that is not switched on, or not yet set up, is shown as such, never as finding no issue (Section 06 §3).', 'C07'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0122', 'APG-S04-DS003', 'bullet', 'For each gap, record the entity and field, the period, the source, the reason (missing, unverified, conflicting, stale, not authoritative, or the underlying record does not exist), the likely holder, the action owner, the approver where one is needed, and the way in that supplies it, saying plainly when that way in is not built.', 'C07'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0122', 'APG-S04-DS004', 'bullet', 'Give each gap a stable identity (entity, field, period and source) and a lifecycle: open, assigned, awaiting evidence, resolved, suppressed, reopened, superseded. A gap found again updates its existing record and nudge; suppression windows and re-notification rules follow Section 06 §9.1.', 'C07'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0122', 'APG-S04-DS005', 'bullet', 'Reassess readiness at setup, after each intake batch or material change of state (combined for a large batch, but prompt), on a schedule, and whenever a record is corrected, quarantined, superseded or revoked. Raise a shared missing setting once, with the projects it affects.', 'C07'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0122', 'APG-S04-DS006', 'bullet', 'An insight may set a tighter freshness limit than its source\'s default for the inputs it depends on; an overall fresh status never hides a stale critical input. Starting thresholds are owner-approved parameters, each with a documented owner and rationale (Section 16 §5), reviewed in the pilot.', 'C09'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0122', 'APG-S04-DS007', 'bullet', 'Show gaps with their factors side by side, as Section 10 §4 requires for findings: the amount affected, urgency, confidence in that amount, whether the person can act now, and what depends on it. A gap is never called a loss or confirmed leakage; any amount comes from a traceable Section 05 calculation or is labelled an estimate.', 'C07'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0122', 'APG-S04-DS008', 'bullet', 'A nudge names the period, the field and the fix, and links to the way in that fixes it only after sign-in; no link lets anyone approve or change data without signing in.', 'C07'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0122', 'APG-S04-DS009', 'bullet', 'At onboarding, show the builder a data checklist: for the systems he uses, which data their export files and a template can supply and which must come another way, with the way in for each; where that is a judgement and not a confirmed sample export, say so.', 'C07'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0122', 'APG-S04-DS010', 'heading 2', '14.2 Telling the builder what is needed — mandatory', 'C08'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0122', 'APG-S04-DS011', 'paragraph', 'Whenever a rule, figure or other insight cannot fully do a check or produce a figure, it must say so: what is missing, why it matters and what the builder is to do. No case may be silent, and nothing may be shown as complete when it is not. Each such message is proven by a test when it is built. A list of the messages, generated by scanning the code, is kept as a controlled artefact and fails when the code gives a message it does not cover.', 'C08'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0148', 'APG-S04-DS012', 'heading 2', '18.1 Ways of supplying data — mandatory', 'C01'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0148', 'APG-S04-DS013', 'paragraph', 'Every fact a person or system supplies, through any way in (import file, document or email, entry screen, setup question, site capture, integration), enters through the intake this section defines, with the same envelope (organisation, project, channel, the person or system, and the time) and the same control checkpoints; nothing writes a supplied fact to the store directly. Records Profit Guardian calculates are written by their calculation runs, with the run recorded (Section 03 §14.3).', 'C01'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0148', 'APG-S04-DS014', 'bullet', 'Every entity in the controlled entity register that this blueprint governs has at least one Level 1 way in that needs no particular builder software: an import template, document or email capture, an entry screen, a setup question, or a record Profit Guardian calculates. Site capture (Level 2) and integrations (Level 3) reduce effort; neither is ever the only way in, and a source system\'s export file through a template stays available when its integration is not.', 'C01'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0148', 'APG-S04-DS015', 'bullet', 'Adding a way in, or a builder changing systems, may change the intake; it must not change any detection rule or financial figure, its logic or its test results. Teaching a rule or figure to use data it does not read today is a change to that rule under its own change request. Where two ways in supply the same field, the Source Authority Register decides which governs, never the most recent arrival.', 'C01'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0148', 'APG-S04-DS016', 'bullet', 'A way in that is not built is never offered to the builder as available.', 'C01'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0148', 'APG-S04-DS017', 'bullet', 'For each kind of record, name its supplier, checker, corrector, approver and the owner accountable if it stays missing. Each role is recorded separately, also where one person holds more than one. Preparing and approving stay separated where Section 02 §3.1 and PG-FR-025 require it, and a keyed value is confirmed by a second person (§18.2), except under the one-person exception of §18.3 (a builder with exactly one authorised person); no other record kind has an exception.', 'C20'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0148', 'APG-S04-DS018', 'heading 2', '18.2 Channel controls — mandatory', 'C03'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0148', 'APG-S04-DS019', 'bullet', 'Email capture verifies the sender and never takes the organisation from the address alone (§6); a verified sender does not make a document genuine or authorised (§5 and §12 still apply). Original messages and attachments are kept.', 'C03'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0148', 'APG-S04-DS020', 'bullet', 'Every uploaded file, attachment and photo is scanned and parsed in isolation within size, archive and resource limits before it is read, and treated as untrusted content (Section 15 §15.9); a malformed or unsupported file is rejected with a reason.', 'C03'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0148', 'APG-S04-DS021', 'bullet', 'Entry screens and setup questions carry the signed-in person, pass the same validation as an imported row, and need approval where the register requires. They never edit a held record: correcting a quarantined or pending record goes through the review workflow (§9, §13).', 'C03'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0148', 'APG-S04-DS022', 'bullet', 'Where a person keys a material value from an uploaded document because no extraction is available, a second person with the verifier role confirms it before it counts. Each value keeps its own confirmation and provenance, also when confirmation is done in batches. Under the one-person exception (§18.3), a builder with exactly one authorised person confirms the values he keyed himself; each such value, and every figure that uses it, permanently carries the marker "confirmed by the person who entered it".', 'C19'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0148', 'APG-S04-DS023', 'bullet', 'Site capture devices are enrolled to the organisation; on a shared device the signed-in user is recorded; the time is checked against the server; each record says how its place was established, and the device location is not assumed reliable. Workers can see what was recorded about them, and a disputed record goes through the correction route (§13). Site capture\'s privacy requirements follow Section 09 §14; they, and the access of a worker (an actor Section 02 §3 does not yet list) to his own records, are settled before site capture is built.', 'C15'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0148', 'APG-S04-DS024', 'bullet', 'A record entered after the event it describes is marked retrospective. A backdated entry never rewrites a result already shown: the earlier result and the records it used stay on record, and the affected insight is reassessed and labelled.', 'C20'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0148', 'APG-S04-DS025', 'heading 2', '18.3 Setup questions — mandatory', 'C04'),
    ('04', 'APG-S04-L0148', 'APG-S04-DS026', 'paragraph', 'Policies, maps, rates and settings the builder sets (the source registry, the Source Authority Register, the cost-code map, users and roles where the platform does not supply them, the financial policy settings the builder owns, namely its status maps, and the rule settings) are supplied through setup questions, versioned, submitted through the intake, and take effect only after approval by the required role. Approval is its own act, with its own permission, approval record (with its rationale and the risks considered, Section 15 §15.11) and audit event, also where the approver is the person who entered the setting. An authorised person, for a kind of record, is a person with the permission to approve that kind of record (for a keyed value, to confirm it); a user who may only capture or view does not count. Where two or more people are authorised for a kind of record, the person who entered a record of that kind cannot approve it. Where exactly one person is authorised for a kind of record listed here (the one-person exception), that person may approve records of that kind: the builder\'s own settings in this paragraph, including the acceptance of a product default (Section 06 §5.1) and users and roles; the builder\'s approved budget and its breakdown (Section 05 §3.3); and the approval steps of a retention event (Section 03 §10.1); and may confirm the values he keyed himself (§18.2). This is a stated policy exception, approved by the owner, to the separation of preparing and approving (Section 02 §3.1, PG-FR-025) and, for these cases only, to Section 15 §15.4\'s separate approval authority and §15.11\'s approval of changes to financial rules, approved baselines, privileged access and retention release. Each record so approved or confirmed, and every figure, finding and report that uses it, permanently carries the marker "approved by the person who entered it" (or "confirmed by the person who entered it" for a keyed value). Records approved under the exception keep their marker; once a second person is authorised for a kind of record, every new record or change of that kind follows the two-person rule, and the exception continues for the other kinds. Every approval, also under the exception, records a short reason (Section 15 checkpoint D). The exception covers nothing else: not the other consequential actions of §15.11 (purchase orders and supplier commitments; contract, scope, specification or material changes; claims, notices and commercial communications; deletion or correction of authoritative evidence; security cancellation), and no action outside Profit Guardian. Onboarding asks only what the insights the builder switches on need. Which calculation methods Profit Guardian supports is product-level policy (Section 05 §3.1 and §5), not a builder setup answer; which supported recognition policy applies to a builder\'s business or project (Section 03 §5.1) is recorded for it and approved as other settings are.', 'C04'),
